  "non_claims": [
    "This is a descriptive comparison of two sampled runs. It does not establish that cfgweather.xml takes precedence over world scripts or engine defaults.",
    "inconclusive_readback does not establish that the engine ignored or failed to apply the candidate's limits; delayed loading, a measurement defect or different getter semantics can produce it. It carries no native conclusion.",
    "candidate_live_limits_read_back states only that the candidate's live limits were read back in every candidate reading and in no stock reading; it does not show why, or that the values follow from them.",
    "The stock run is not required to show a forecast cycle; its controller behaviour is not characterised.",
    "Values inside or outside the limits, and forecasts outside them, do not show a cause; engine limits and world-script forecasts can coexist.",
    "candidate_current_read_back states only that, in the candidate run, the first forecast equalled the candidate's <current> actual, the first countdown was about time plus duration minus the weather time, and the actual reached that value by about time, while the stock run's first forecast did not equal it. current_inconclusive carries no native conclusion and does not mean the engine ignored <current>. The tolerances are provisional.",
    "Actual values outside the limits before the actual first reaches the initial forecast (or before the first scheduled change) are reported as an initial transition, not counted as violations; this does not show how the engine starts from a pre-existing state.",
    "Two single runs sample random weather. Nothing here is runtime acceptance; runtime acceptance and feature enablement stay pending."
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Values inside the candidate's limits are reported separately (values_in_range) from the live limit readback; world-script forecasts and engine limits can coexist.",
    "Phenomena the candidate does not change are not_treated: reported, never gating.",
    "Whether the engine sets mission_weather for enable=1 is read from the flags above only."
  ],
